-- title:
--   Borel-fixed field of the level automorphisms: the case q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota_0 : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota_0(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $q^2M'$ and group $H = \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise images of all ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ (with $p_g$ giving a nonzero series). Let $\tau : \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \to (K \simeq_L K)$ be any function such that for each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the automorphism $\tau(\gamma)$ satisfies [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) for the data $L$, $q$, $\zeta$, $q$, $q^2M'$, $H$ and the element $\gamma^{-1}$: for every weight $k$, every pair of forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ ($\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g \neq 0$), every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image of $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota_*(\tau(\gamma)x)\cdot q\text{-}\mathrm{exp}\big(g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}\big) = q\text{-}\mathrm{exp}\big(f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}\big)$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\delta = \begin{pmatrix} a & b/m \\ mc & d\end{pmatrix}$ for $\delta = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d\end{pmatrix}$. Then for every $w \in K$: $\tau(\gamma)w = w$ for all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ whose upper-right entry is divisible by $q$ if and only if the Laurent series underlying $w$ lies in [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) $\mathbb{Q}\,\Gamma_0(qM')$, the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms on $\Gamma_0(qM')$.
--
--   This identifies the common fixed field of the level automorphisms indexed by the Borel-type subgroup $\{\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') : q \mid \gamma_{01}\}$ as the base change to $L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(qM')$, in the case $q = 2$ (a companion to the same assertion for larger $q$). It feeds the computation of the comap of the relevant places, the ramification index one statement and separability over the Gauss point for the $\Gamma_0(qM')$-level curve.
